---
/** Pipeline of the Email Assistant, drawn from the repo's main.py and call_gemini.py. Colours are design tokens. */
---

<figure class="not-prose my-10">
  {/* eslint-disable astro/jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-tabindex -- scrollable on phones, must be keyboard-reachable */}
  <div
    class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line bg-cream-soft p-4 sm:p-6"
    tabindex="0"
    role="region"
    aria-label="Pipeline diagram (scrolls sideways on small screens)"
  >
    {/* eslint-enable astro/jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-tabindex */}
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 760 330"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="ea-title ea-desc"
      class="h-auto w-full min-w-[34rem] font-sans"
    >
      <title id="ea-title">Email Assistant pipeline</title>
      <desc id="ea-desc">
        A FastAPI endpoint fetches the 5 latest Gmail messages. Each email gets a profanity check, then four Gemini 2.5
        Flash calls: sentiment, summary, a JSON classification of the summary into urgency, intent and topic, and a
        draft reply. The email is embedded with all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and stored in ChromaDB; the most similar past email's
        reply is retrieved and given to Gemini as a tone example. An auto-reply flag is set when the email is not urgent
        and not FYI. A second endpoint sends a reply through the Gmail API.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="ea-arrow"
          viewBox="0 0 10 10"
          refX="9"
          refY="5"
          markerWidth="7"
          markerHeight="7"
          orient="auto-start-reverse"
        >
          <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" fill="var(--color-forest)"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <style>
        .box {
          fill: var(--color-cream);
          stroke: var(--color-forest);
          stroke-width: 1.5;
        }
        .key {
          fill: var(--color-cream);
          stroke: var(--color-pink);
          stroke-width: 3;
        }
        .t {
          fill: var(--color-forest);
          font-size: 15px;
          font-weight: 600;
        }
        .s {
          fill: var(--color-forest-muted);
          font-size: 12.5px;
        }
        .a {
          stroke: var(--color-forest);
          stroke-width: 1.5;
          fill: none;
          marker-end: url(#ea-arrow);
        }
      </style>

      <rect class="box" x="10" y="30" width="150" height="74" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="24" y="56">
        Gmail API
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="24" y="78">
        5 latest inbox
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="24" y="93">
        messages (OAuth)
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="190" y="30" width="150" height="74" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="204" y="56">
        Guardrail
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="204" y="78">
        profanity flag
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="204" y="93">
        (better-profanity)
      </text>

      <rect class="key" x="370" y="10" width="220" height="140" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="384" y="36">
        Gemini 2.5 Flash
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="60">
        1. sentiment
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="80">
        2. summary
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="100">
        3. classify summary → JSON
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="116">
        {" "}
        urgency · intent · topic
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="136">
        4. draft reply
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="370" y="200" width="220" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="384" y="226">
        ChromaDB (local)
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="248">
        all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="266">
        top-1 similar email's reply
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="384" y="282">
        → tone example for step 4
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="620" y="30" width="130" height="104" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="634" y="56">
        FastAPI
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="634" y="78">
        auto-reply flag:
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="634" y="93">
        not urgent and
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="634" y="108">
        not FYI
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="620" y="200" width="130" height="74" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="634" y="226">
        Send reply
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="634" y="248">
        via Gmail API
      </text>

      <path class="a" d="M160 67 H186"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M340 67 H366"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M590 80 H616"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M480 196 V154"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M685 134 V196"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M265 104 V245 H366"></path>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-forest-muted">
    One request processes up to 5 emails, one after another. Drawn from <code>main.py</code> and
    <code>call_gemini.py</code>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
